00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Eddie Cusack's a good cop having a very bad day.

2
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Code of Silence is a action, crime, drama film directed by Andrew Davis.

3
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:12,000
A Chicago cop is caught in the middle of a gang war while his own comrades
shun him because he wants to take an irresponsible cop down.

4
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Eddie Cusack, played by Chuck Norris.

5
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Tony Luna, played by Mike Genovese.

6
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Luis Comacho, played by Henry Silva.

7
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Commander Kates, played by Bert Remsen.

8
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Cragie, played by Ralph Foody.

9
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Felix Scalese, played by Nathan Davis.

10
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Code of Silence is a 1985 American neo noir action thriller film
directed by Andrew Davis and starring Chuck Norris.

11
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:08,000
The cast includes  Molly Hagan, Henry Silva, Ralph
Foody, Bert Remsen, and Dennis Farina.

12
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
The screenplay is credited to Michael Butler, Dennis Shryack, and Mike Gray.

13
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:52,000
In Chicago’s Uptown neighborhood, Sergeant Eddie Cusack (Norris) leads a sting operation against a gang
but the plan goes awry, resulting in a shootout where several are killed or wounded.

14
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:14,000
Cusack is ostracized for refusing to support a corrupt
cop who killed an innocent bystander.

15
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Meanwhile, the family of a mob boss is killed, except for
his daughter Diana (Hagan), by a rival gang.

16
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:58,000
Cusack, despite being isolated by his department, works to
protect Diana and bring the criminals to justice.

17
00:57:14,000 --> 00:57:20,000
Originally written as a potential fourth Dirty Harry film, the screenplay by Michael Butler and Dennis Shryack
passed through multiple hands before being purchased by Orion Pictures for $800,000 in 1983.

18
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
After several high-profile actors turned down the lead role, Chuck Norris was cast in 1984, marking
a departure from his usual martial arts films and helping to legitimize his career.

19
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:04,000
The production, directed by Chicago native Andrew Davis, was filmed extensively
on location in Chicago, showcasing several iconic landmarks.

20
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Molly Hagan, cast straight out of drama school, found the experience formative for her career, while Dennis Farina, then a Chicago
police officer, credited the film as a significant break that helped launch his transition into full-time acting.

21
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
The film was released by Orion Pictures on May 3, 1985, and received generally positive reviews,
with critics praising its slick direction, strong performances, and engaging action.

22
01:14:04,000 --> 01:14:10,000
It was regarded as a standout in Chuck Norris's career, with
many considering it his best film to date.

23
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:32,000
The film was noted for its heavy-duty thriller elements, stylish urban
setting, and sensational stunts, all contributing to its appeal.

24
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
While some saw it as a successful bid by Norris to reach a broader audience, others highlighted the gritty, realistic feel of the film,
drawing favorable comparisons to earlier gritty cop films, particularly in contrast to more cartoonish action movies.

25
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:16,000
The film was recognized for offering genuine human
interest alongside its action-packed sequences.

26
01:27:32,000 --> 01:27:38,000
The film debuted at number 1 with an opening weekend gross of $5.5 million and
ultimately earned a total of $20.3 million at the US box office.

27
01:30:54,000 --> 01:31:00,000
Andrew Davis credits the success of the film for
turning him into an action film director.

28
01:34:16,000 --> 01:34:22,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, police, undercover, hitman, fight.

29
01:37:38,000 --> 01:37:44,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
